  "description": "A very large black horse of the snowfields with a rack of antlers on mare and stallion alike, swept back and over with a tine thrown forward above the face, the same on both sides. Half of them are grulla - dun over the black, smoke-grey with a dark stripe down the back - a quarter go grey with age, and a quarter carry silver, which turns a black mane and tail to flax. Some carry moss on the tines, and a few have points that glow through the polar night. Untroubled by any cold.",
