  "notes": [
    "BLACK UNDER EVERYTHING (owner's spec, 2026-10-01). Every founder is E/E a/a. Half are dun - D/D in 20, D/d2 in 30 - which on black is grulla. A quarter are grey, G2/N and G3/N evenly. A quarter carry silver (Z/z), which on a black horse shows: a flaxen mane and tail and a lighter body. The three loci are independent, so a grulla can also be grey or silver.",
    "A SPRINKLE OF WHITE (owner's spec). About one in twenty carries exactly one copy of one natural white allele - any of all fifty-four, across natural zebra, roan, rabicano, tobiano, leopard, frame, every KIT allele, manchado, the MITF and PAX3 splashes and the two PATN modifiers - each at an equal share. PATN1 and PATN2 show nothing without leopard, and a recessive like manchado is carried silently. Because the loci are rolled independently a very few carry two.",
    "ANTLERS ON BOTH SEXES. Every founder carries Ant, the allele that grows antlers on a mare as well as a stallion. One in five also carries the stallion-only Antm silently: Ant is dominant over it, so it only surfaces when two Rimeharts each pass it on, and then the mares of that line go bare.",
    "BROW-TINED, AND SYMMETRIC (owner's spec). 70 in 100 are Brw/Brw; 15 carry Frk under it and show brow-tined anyway, and 15 carry Pal over it and show palmate. No asymmetry band, so every rack matches itself, as every wild one does.",
    "SIZE AND TINES ARE BANDED UP. Racks sit from small to large with three and a half to six and a half tines; a line bred for size climbs to a massive rack, and the clamp stops it there.",
    "VERY LARGE (owner's spec): a draught horse's size band, Clydesdale-tall at the top.",
    "Moss on every one that blooms (growth index 1), and a fifth carry the bloom silently. A tenth have glowing points, and another fifth carry them. Cold-tolerant (Ctol/Ctol) on every horse; spawns only in snow biomes."
  ]
